      },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Which city is the capital of Australia's state with Rottnest-free Gold Coast? Gold Coast's nearest capital.\",\n          \"answer\": \"Brisbane\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Which Victorian national park is mainland Australia's southernmost point?\",\n          \"answer\": \"Wilsons Promontory\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"round\": 5,\n      \"genre\": \"film\",\n      \"difficulty\": 2,\n      \"region\": \"au\",\n      \"count\": 4,\n      \"correct_rate\": 0.8,\n      \"questions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Which Australian actress played Princess Diana in 'The Crown' and appeared in 'Tenet' (2020)?\",\n          \"options\": [\n            \"Elizabeth Debicki\",\n            \"Teresa Palmer\",\n            \"Mia Wasikowska\",\n            \"Yvonne Strahovski\"\n          ],\n          \"answer\": \"Elizabeth Debicki\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"In the 2015 family film 'Paper Planes', a boy from Western Australia travels to the world paper plane championships in which country?\",\n          \"options\": [\n            \"China\",\n            \"Japan\",\n            \"France\",\n            \"United States\"\n          ],\n          \"answer\": \"Japan\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"In Greg McLean's 'Rogue' (2007), tourists in the Northern Territory are stalked by what giant animal?\",\n          \"answer\": \"Crocodile\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Decades before the cartoon dog, 'Bluey' was a 1976 Crawford police drama. Who played the title detective?\",\n          \"options\": [\n            \"Jack Thompson\",\n            \"Lucky Grills\",\n            \"Gerard Kennedy\",\n            \"Leonard Teale\"\n          ],\n          \"answer\": \"Lucky Grills\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"round\": 6,\n      \"genre\": \"sport\",\n      \"difficulty\": 3,\n      \"region\": \"au\",\n      \"count\": 4,\n      \"correct_rate\": 0.55,\n      \"questions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Which Australian cyclist won the Tour de France green jersey in 2002, 2003 and 2004?\",\n          \"answer\": \"Robbie McEwen\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Australian golfer Jason Day won his first major championship in 2015. Which one?\",\n          \"answer\": \"US PGA Championship\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Raelene Boyle won Olympic silver medals in 1968 and 1972 in which sport?\",\n          \"answer\": \"Athletics\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Kim Brennan won Rio 2016 rowing gold in which boat?\",\n          \"options\": [\n            \"Quad sculls\",\n            \"Coxless pair\",\n            \"Single sculls\",\n            \"Double sculls\"\n          ],\n          \"answer\": \"Single sculls\",\n          \"marks\": [\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Quizzly Bears\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Les Quizerables\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"Opera House Party\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"team\": \"The Blow-Ins\",\n              \"answer\": \"\",\n              \"correct\": true\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"# Venue notes (Sydney, Australia)\\n\\n- Country/region: Australia, use region `au` (plus global if needed).\\n- Format: the trivia master has chosen 6 rounds of 4 two nights running (default is 5 x 8; ask or confirm). The bank records answers as each round is served, so no answer sheet comes back: check round_summary after each round. The trivia master may not reply during the night, so run straight through.\\n- Genres: crowd loves film (the trivia master says so; film at level 2 scored 75-80%, at level 3 about 50-65%). Science and geography were OK at level 2 (~60%). Sport at 3 was 55%. Music and history were hard at level 3 (40-45%) and have not been tried at level 2: give them a turn next week at level 2.\\n- Difficulty: level 3 is too hard for this room across genres (~50-55%). Level 2 gives ~60-80%, about right. Start next night at 2 and only step up when a round is over 75%. Even film should start at 2.\\n- Quirk: the bank sometimes returns garbled question text; read it sensibly and tell the room.\\n\"\n}\n"
          },
