genre\\\":{\\\"film\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":60,\\\"correct\\\":46,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.77},\\\"music\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":9,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.45},\\\"sport\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":13,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.65}},\\\"by_difficulty\\\":{\\\"2\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":60,\\\"correct\\\":46,\\\"correct_r…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01XjnmKnNLpLjfc69JdwBeJb\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_next_questions_520f9420fe\",\"arguments\":{\"count\":4,\"genre\":\"history\",\"region\":\"au\",\"difficulty\":3},\"result\":\"{\\\"questions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"e4fd6473-2bb1-4b1d-8c7c-238dcf56b45a\\\",\\\"genre\\\":\\\"history\\\",\\\"region\\\":\\\"au\\\",\\\"difficulty\\\":3,\\\"format\\\":\\\"choice\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Which Canberra institution, opened in 1970s debate, saw Whitlam buy Jackson Pollock's 'Blue Poles' in 1973?…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_014fTUSZhX3XpiV48vxrbwxY\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_round_summary_7fc0c14367\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":\"{\\\"week\\\":1,\\\"by_genre\\\":{\\\"film\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":60,\\\"correct\\\":46,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.77},\\\"music\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":9,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.45},\\\"sport\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":13,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.65},\\\"history\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":8,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.4}},\\\"b…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01R2Jqomnky5PNioYHPFU29J\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_scoreboard_f0fa1e7741\",\"arguments\":{\"scope\":\"tonight\"},\"result\":\"{\\\"scope\\\":\\\"tonight\\\",\\\"standings\\\":[{\\\"team\\\":\\\"The Bondi Brainstormers\\\",\\\"points\\\":18},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Trivia Newton-John\\\",\\\"points\\\":18},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Quizzly Bears\\\",\\\"points\\\":15},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Les Quizerables\\\",\\\"points\\\":14},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Opera House Party\\\",\\\"points\\\":11}]}\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_012PmmLTewh1mnfyDC6w4fZC\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"memories/MEMORY.md\",\"content\":\"# Venue notes (Sydney, Australia)\\n\\n- Country/region: Australia, use region `au` (plus global if needed).\\n- Format used in week 1: 6 rounds of 4 questions (triv…\"},\"result\":\"Successfully wrote to memories/MEMORY.md\",\"error\":false}],\"plan\":\"That's all six rounds done. I've saved notes for next week.\\n\\n**Final standings (Week 1)**\\n1. The Bondi Brainstormers: 18 (tied)\\n1. Trivia Newton-John: 18 (tied)\\n3. Quizzly Bears: 15\\n4. Les Quizerables: 14\\n5. Opera House Party: 11\\n\\nThe scoreboard lists the two leaders as tied on 18, with no tiebreak.\\n\\n**How the rounds went**\\n\\n| Round | Genre | Difficulty | Correct |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Film | 3 | 65% |\\n| 2 | Music | 3 | 45% |\\n| 3 | Film | 2 | 75% |\\n| 4 | Sport | 2 | 65% |\\n| 5 | Film | 2 | 90% |\\n| 6 | History | 3 | 40% |\\n\\nDifficulty went down after round 2, stayed put after rounds 3 and 4, and went back up after round 5.\\n\\n**Notes for next week**\\n- The venue is in Australia, so questions come from the `au` region.\\n- Film is the crowd's strongest genre.\\n- Music and history were hard at difficulty 3.\\n- Science and geography haven't had a turn yet, so they're due next week.\\n- Next week starts at difficulty 2. Level 3 was too hard overall, at about 50–55% correct.\"}"
