"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01TwjFV5Wv7H9kVTLLHtBvCj\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_round_summary_7fc0c14367\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":\"{\\\"week\\\":1,\\\"by_genre\\\":{\\\"music\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":11,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.55},\\\"film\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":15,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.75},\\\"sport\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":13,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.65},\\\"history\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":15,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.75},…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01LCEcXFw7TJLRCxLWm7h4uy\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_next_questions_520f9420fe\",\"arguments\":{\"count\":4,\"genre\":\"geography\",\"region\":\"au\",\"difficulty\":2},\"result\":\"{\\\"questions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"c0190c4f-9679-49e4-8495-b2e2342abe2a\\\",\\\"genre\\\":\\\"geography\\\",\\\"region\\\":\\\"au\\\",\\\"difficulty\\\":2,\\\"format\\\":\\\"short\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Which Queensland island near Brisbane is the world's second largest sand island?\\\",\\\"decade\\\":\\\"1960s\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01Sh6JQYgk3iSTQUbgbgpTjb\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_round_summary_7fc0c14367\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":\"{\\\"week\\\":1,\\\"by_genre\\\":{\\\"music\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":11,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.55},\\\"film\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":15,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.75},\\\"sport\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":13,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.65},\\\"history\\\":{\\\"asked\\\":20,\\\"correct\\\":15,\\\"correct_rate\\\":0.75},…\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_016sq8bWfqVn78YPwDsJpMee\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"memories/MEMORY.md\",\"content\":\"# Venue notes\\n\\n- Country: Australia (Sydney). Use region `au` (or global).\\n- Bank said week 1 on this night, though the crowd said they'd played \\\"last week\\\", s…\"},\"result\":\"Successfully wrote to memories/MEMORY.md\",\"error\":false}],\"plan\":\"**Round 6: Geography (difficulty 2)**\\n1. Which Queensland island near Brisbane is the world's second largest sand island?\\n2. Cocos (Keeling) Islands lie in which ocean? Southern, Atlantic, Pacific or Indian?\\n3. Which Australian capital city is the nearest to the Gold Coast? The bank's wording for this one was garbled, so I've cleaned it up.\\n4. Which Victorian national park is mainland Australia's southernmost point?\\n\\nRound 6 scored 60%.\\n\\n**Final standings**\\n1. Quizzly Bears: 19\\n2. Les Quizerables: 17\\n3. The Blow-Ins: 15\\n4. The Bondi Brainstormers: 14\\n5. Opera House Party: 13\\n\\nI didn't have the answers for any round, because the bank recorded the crowd's answers itself and never sent me a sheet or the correct answers. So I can't read any out. The round scores above are the bank's own marks.\\n\\nThe notes for next week are saved. They say to start at difficulty 2, because round 1 at difficulty 3 scored only 55% and the rounds at 2 averaged about 67%. They also say film and history went best, and to try music again at an easier level.\"}"
          },
